    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ab39e356-ee67-569a-a5c6-fae3d566e2bc",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a47a4f05-f18f-5257-b00c-da9bbd4598b9",
